# CPX - Manage command processor extensions

```text
CPX LIST
CPX LOAD name
CPX UNLOAD name
```

## Inspect commands

CPX LIST shows active command packages in search order. The standard RCP
package supplies resident commands including DIR, COPY and MOVE. To run
a transient explicitly, put a colon before its name, as in :DIR.

## Load a package

```text
CPX LOAD RCP
CPX LIST
```

Use LOAD to restore RCP if it has been unloaded. Keep RCP.CPX accessible
in A0. For resident terminal or clock services, use [RSX](RSX.HLP).
